  "rendered_prompt": "<s><|im_start|>system\nYou are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nParagraph:\n\"\"\"\nIn To Kill a Mockingbird, Atticus Finch shows that doing the right thing is not always easy. He agrees to defend Tom Robinson even though he knows that most people in Maycomb will be angry at him. Atticus is someone who never gives up on what he believes, even when his own children get bullied at school because of it. He tells Scout that you never really understand a person until you look at things from their point of view. This shows that he wants his kids to be fair to everyone, not just people who are like them. Atticus is a good example of a person who stays brave when it would be easier to stay quiet.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer selected this text:\n\"\"\"\nThis shows that he wants his kids to be fair to everyone, not just people who are like them.\n\"\"\"\n\nGive 5 different rewrites of the selected text that use new wording but keep about the same length. Keep the meaning, facts, names, numbers and quotations. Each rewrite must read naturally in place of the original. Put the best options first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
